  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Ledger in Daylight",
    "overview": "\n**Creative North Star: \"The Ledger in Daylight\"**\n\nA light, dense analytics app in the category's own register: white ground, slate ink, hairline borders, one indigo accent. Every surface is a working instrument (KPI tile, chart card, bar list, sortable table), and every number carries its source and date. No themed metaphor, no decorative imagery; the only pictures are listing thumbnails inside table rows.\n\nDensity is high and even: 13px body, 32px controls, 14px gaps between cards. Hierarchy comes from weight and size inside one family, not from color. Color is a data channel with fixed meanings, so it is spent sparingly and never for decoration.\n\nThe interface is bilingual FR/EN through a toggle in the sidebar foot, with French number formatting (thin-space thousands, `%` after a space). Motion is minimal: a 260ms rise on page sections, 120ms hover fades, a 1.2s skeleton shimmer, all off under reduced motion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White canvas, slate-tinted neutrals, 1px hairlines carry all structure.",
      "One indigo accent for data marks and selected state only.",
      "Green/red reserved for price direction; amber reserved for stale data.",
      "Inter with tabular figures everywhere; numbers align in columns.",
      "Persistent 232px sidebar on desktop, sticky blurred top bar with underline tabs on mobile."
    ],
    "rules": [
